### 5d. Stability check

RK4 is stable on `y' = λy` when `|λ|Δt < 2.785` (negative real `λ`). For this system `λ` comes from the Jacobian of `[v, a]` with respect to `[h, v]`:

$$\mathbf J = \begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\ \dfrac{D}{mH} & -\dfrac{\rho\, C_D A\,|v|}{m}\end{bmatrix}.$$

For each flight we evaluate the eigenvalues along the whole trajectory and multiply the largest `|λ|` by the **largest** step used (conservative).
def stability_number(tb, m0):
    """Return (max |lambda| along the trajectory [1/s], max |lambda| * dt_max)."""
    f = simulate(tb, m0=m0, keep_traj=True)
    t, h, v = f.traj_t, f.traj_y[:, iH], f.traj_y[:, iV]
    mass = m0 - mp * np.minimum(t, tb) / tb
    rho  = rho0 * np.exp(-h / H)
    a_v  = -rho * CD * A * np.abs(v) / mass                  # d(accel)/dv
    a_h  = 0.5 * rho * CD * A * v * np.abs(v) / (H * mass)   # d(accel)/dh  = D/(m H)
    disc = np.sqrt((a_v**2 + 4 * a_h).astype(complex))       # eigenvalues of [[0,1],[a_h,a_v]]
    lam  = np.maximum(np.abs((a_v + disc) / 2), np.abs((a_v - disc) / 2))
    dt_max = max((tb - t_ramp) / N_BURN, DT_COAST)
    return lam.max(), lam.max() * dt_max


results = [(m0, tb, *stability_number(tb, m0)) for m0 in m_values for tb in burn_times[::7]]
m_w, tb_w, lam_w, sn_w = max(results, key=lambda r: r[3])
print(f"Worst case over {len(results)} flights: m0 = {m_w} kg, tb = {tb_w:.2f} s")
print(f"  max |lambda| = {lam_w:.3f} 1/s,  |lambda|*dt = {sn_w:.4f}  (limit 2.785)")
